      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}\\tan  (x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,3^{x} \\sec^{2}{\\left(x \\right)}$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={3}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\tan  (x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({3}^{x})}^{′}\\tan  (x)+{3}^{x}{(\\tan  (x))}^{′} \\\\  & =({3}^{x}\\ln  (3))\\tan  (x)+{3}^{x}(\\sec ^{2} (x)) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\ln  (3)\\tan  (x)+{3}^{x}\\sec ^{2} (x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
